1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
And yet she did grant my wish.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Holding up her end of this perverse contract, I suppose.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,000
And I became an eternal girl.

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,000
To repeat the cycle.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Get it now?

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,000
That's the ugly truth behind this game!

7
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:30,000
He's away!

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,000
He's away!

9
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,000
He's away!

10
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Oh my gosh! Are you okay?

11
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Ruko!

12
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Go get help! Call an ambulance!

13
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:52,000
But I don't have a cell phone!

14
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Come on, think!

15
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Hitoi has one! Just hurry!

16
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,000
What? Oh, right!

17
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,000
It's fine.

18
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,000
An election or anything.

19
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Willi's world may begin.

20
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,000
You don't remember the Ar Wild processes.

21
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:18,000
I'm super jealous.

22
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:21,700
I gave her flash.

23
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:23,000
May have%.

24
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:25,000
It's IU's history men who will believe you

25
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,000
after a trip.

26
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,000
It's alright!

27
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:31,000
It's not THAT CHADCasEhe.

28
00:01:31,000 --> 00:02:00,980
Thank you.

29
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:30,980
Thank you.

30
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:34,920
Yeah, nothing serious. The doctor said she's stable now.

31
00:02:36,220 --> 00:02:46,620
Uh-huh. Yeah, they called them. I hope this is okay. But I, uh, I wanted to wait with Hitaway a bit longer. You know, until her parents show up, at least.

32
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:56,240
Sure. That's fine. Of course you can stay with your friend. I'm just glad you called. But how are you?

33
00:02:56,840 --> 00:02:57,860
I'm worried.

34
00:02:59,660 --> 00:03:05,060
No, don't. I'll be okay. I'll call again if anything else comes up.

35
00:03:05,060 --> 00:03:06,980
Mm-hmm.

36
00:03:06,980 --> 00:03:27,860
Why didn't I listen to you?

37
00:03:27,860 --> 00:03:34,160
I should have stopped when I had the chance.

38
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:37,180
Oh, Yuzuki. Do you know how this happened?

39
00:03:37,480 --> 00:03:42,940
I think so. I won the battle and then... Well, it was strange.

40
00:03:42,940 --> 00:03:46,940
And now...

41
00:03:46,940 --> 00:03:49,420
You become an Elric.

42
00:03:49,420 --> 00:03:57,260
Where am I?

43
00:04:04,880 --> 00:04:06,680
What's going on here?

44
00:04:06,680 --> 00:04:08,600
Nice to meet you.

45
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:14,320
Yuzuki.

46
00:04:17,980 --> 00:04:19,400
Who are you?

47
00:04:19,940 --> 00:04:20,680
My name is...

48
00:04:21,620 --> 00:04:22,120
Mayu.

49
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:26,740
That's insane.

50
00:04:27,420 --> 00:04:29,220
It was like some sort of weird initiation.

51
00:04:29,940 --> 00:04:33,460
She told me all about selectors, Elrigs, and how Eternal Girls work.

52
00:04:33,960 --> 00:04:37,320
If you become an Elrig, then apparently you wake up there.

53
00:04:38,060 --> 00:04:40,080
You think Hanayu went through the same thing?

54
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:41,380
I would imagine so.

55
00:04:42,340 --> 00:04:44,320
Mayu. A white room.

56
00:04:44,980 --> 00:04:46,840
Tama, do you know something?

57
00:04:47,500 --> 00:04:49,540
My memory is still too fuzzy.

58
00:04:49,980 --> 00:04:51,980
So who is this Mayu girl?

59
00:04:53,100 --> 00:04:55,380
I don't know. She didn't talk about herself much.

60
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:56,480
I see.

61
00:04:57,560 --> 00:04:58,920
I know what you're thinking.

62
00:04:59,300 --> 00:05:01,560
That Hanayu was tricking me this entire time.

63
00:05:02,640 --> 00:05:06,020
She didn't mention a word about her taking my place or any of that.

64
00:05:06,440 --> 00:05:10,780
If what Mayu told me is true, she's out there living my life right now.

65
00:05:11,780 --> 00:05:13,960
All that talk about helping me with my wish.

66
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:16,320
Figured she was laughing at me the whole time.

67
00:05:16,320 --> 00:05:17,280
Don't say that!

68
00:05:17,340 --> 00:05:18,380
Well, that's what I thought.

69
00:05:20,760 --> 00:05:21,440
But...

70
00:05:21,440 --> 00:05:22,420
Hanayu...

71
00:05:22,420 --> 00:05:24,620
How could you do this?

72
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:26,100
We were friends!

73
00:05:26,620 --> 00:05:27,640
Don't blame her.

74
00:05:28,340 --> 00:05:31,260
Elrigs are not allowed to share the truth with their selectors.

75
00:05:31,500 --> 00:05:33,300
Why do you know this and nobody else?

76
00:05:33,960 --> 00:05:35,240
What is this place?

77
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:36,580
What the hell are you?

78
00:05:36,580 --> 00:05:45,480
If this rule is broken, if their selector learns the truth and refuses to battle anymore,

79
00:05:45,920 --> 00:05:50,200
that Elrig will forever lose her chance to escape the world inside her card.

80
00:05:50,200 --> 00:05:54,380
Then you're doing it too.

81
00:05:54,380 --> 00:05:56,380
You're trying to trick...

82
00:05:56,380 --> 00:05:58,380
Poor Hitoye.

83
00:05:58,740 --> 00:06:00,060
It's not that simple.

84
00:06:00,900 --> 00:06:02,100
I'll try to explain.

85
00:06:02,100 --> 00:06:11,980
Nice to meet you, selector.

86
00:06:13,660 --> 00:06:15,120
I couldn't believe it.

87
00:06:15,580 --> 00:06:18,300
Hitoye became a selector again and I was her Elrig.

88
00:06:18,300 --> 00:06:20,880
I didn't know what to do.

89
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:22,760
Should I hide the truth from her?

90
00:06:23,520 --> 00:06:25,460
Was it my job to force her into battle?

91
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:30,480
At the very least, I knew I'd be stuck in this card if I didn't.

92
00:06:31,640 --> 00:06:33,300
But after what happened...

93
00:06:33,300 --> 00:06:36,980
Let's be friends, Hitoye.

94
00:06:37,520 --> 00:06:38,480
How do...

95
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:39,680
How do you know my name?

96
00:06:40,260 --> 00:06:41,060
Who are you?

97
00:06:41,440 --> 00:06:43,740
Well, let's just say I'm magic, okay?

98
00:06:48,160 --> 00:06:49,960
Even though we didn't know her for long,

99
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:51,960
I still felt like we were good friends.

100
00:06:52,520 --> 00:06:54,020
But after her wish was corrupted,

101
00:06:54,220 --> 00:06:55,840
she really did forget about us.

102
00:06:56,740 --> 00:06:59,040
I'm your Elrig now, so take good care of me.

103
00:07:00,200 --> 00:07:00,680
Elrig?

104
00:07:01,280 --> 00:07:01,720
What?

105
00:07:01,720 --> 00:07:04,160
For starters, can you tell me your wish?

106
00:07:06,460 --> 00:07:07,380
My wish?

107
00:07:08,280 --> 00:07:10,360
Yeah, if you have one, I can make it come true.

108
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:12,260
I'm Yuzuki, by the way.

109
00:07:12,840 --> 00:07:15,000
I think you and I will be good friends.

110
00:07:15,520 --> 00:07:15,800
You.

111
00:07:16,100 --> 00:07:16,520
Su.

112
00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:17,380
Ki.

113
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:24,480
I've gotta fight my way out of here.

114
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:27,600
Even if I have to hurt Hitoye to do it,

115
00:07:28,200 --> 00:07:30,080
I need to see Kazuki again.

116
00:07:30,080 --> 00:07:32,200
That was all I could think.

117
00:07:34,200 --> 00:07:35,720
Hey, don't be shy.

118
00:07:36,340 --> 00:07:37,520
You must have a wish.

119
00:07:37,520 --> 00:07:40,200
I don't know.

120
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:40,320
I don't know.

121
00:07:42,880 --> 00:07:43,480
Hitoye?

122
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:44,780
You okay?

123
00:07:45,400 --> 00:07:46,340
Did something happen?

124
00:07:47,020 --> 00:07:48,160
Talk to me, Hitoye.

125
00:07:48,240 --> 00:07:48,680
Please!

126
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:52,020
I knew her wish was already dead.

127
00:07:52,020 --> 00:07:53,860
But what could I do?

128
00:07:54,940 --> 00:07:57,280
This was the only chance given to me.

129
00:07:57,960 --> 00:07:59,160
I had to take it.

130
00:08:00,620 --> 00:08:02,020
But then...

131
00:08:02,020 --> 00:08:08,660
Just as I was starting to think I'd have to give up,

132
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:11,460
I guess I got lucky and...

133
00:08:11,460 --> 00:08:12,400
Something happened.

134
00:08:12,400 --> 00:08:12,460
I guess I got lucky and something happened.

135
00:08:12,460 --> 00:08:15,720
Let's go.

136
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:29,080
Hitoye?

137
00:08:29,080 --> 00:08:35,080
Oh my gosh, are you okay?

138
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:39,080
If it hurts, why are you putting yourself through this?

139
00:08:39,080 --> 00:08:46,080
I don't know why. I just feel like this is something important.

140
00:08:46,080 --> 00:08:53,080
But I think maybe I do have a wish.

141
00:08:53,080 --> 00:09:04,080
I want to have friends. And for some reason, that hurts.

142
00:09:04,080 --> 00:09:12,080
After all the horrible things she went through, all that pain and confusion,

143
00:09:12,080 --> 00:09:18,080
she still asks for the same thing.

144
00:09:18,080 --> 00:09:24,080
Can I have friends? Can you do that?

145
00:09:36,080 --> 00:09:41,080
You have my word. I promise I'll make your wish come true.

146
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:45,080
How could I say no to a crying girl, you know?

147
00:09:45,080 --> 00:09:49,080
Whether it was right or not, I guess I got caught up in the moment.

148
00:09:49,080 --> 00:10:00,080
Will Hitoy's wish turn out like mine?

149
00:10:00,080 --> 00:10:04,080
Even if I can make it come true, is it really worth the cost?

150
00:10:04,080 --> 00:10:09,080
It makes me wonder if Hanayou went through all this too.

151
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:13,080
I wonder if she felt as lost and hurt as I do now.

152
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:17,080
And if her wish came true...

153
00:10:17,080 --> 00:10:19,080
Harayou...

154
00:10:24,080 --> 00:10:28,080
After that, I started to rethink things.

155
00:10:28,080 --> 00:10:30,080
Hey, Hito-e?

156
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:36,080
If you want your wish to come true, we'll have to find a battle.

157
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:38,080
Okay, I'll try.

158
00:10:38,080 --> 00:10:41,080
I intentionally had her battle you.

159
00:10:41,080 --> 00:10:44,080
And then told you the truth in front of her.

160
00:10:44,080 --> 00:10:46,080
So it's not quite what it looked like.

161
00:10:46,080 --> 00:10:49,080
I was hoping she'd refuse to fight after she heard that.

162
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:53,080
But if she quit, then you'd be stuck in the cart forever, wouldn't you?

163
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:55,080
That doesn't matter.

164
00:10:55,080 --> 00:10:57,080
She's my friend.

165
00:10:57,080 --> 00:11:02,080
If I have to sacrifice her, then I might as well just disappear.

166
00:11:02,080 --> 00:11:08,080
And besides, if I can't live as Yuzuki Kurabayashi anymore,

167
00:11:08,080 --> 00:11:12,080
if I can't even love Kazuki as myself anymore,

168
00:11:12,080 --> 00:11:14,080
then what's the point?

169
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:15,080
I give up.

170
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:16,080
Yuzuki?

171
00:11:16,080 --> 00:11:17,080
Hito-e?

172
00:11:17,080 --> 00:11:20,080
Uh, hello!

173
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:22,080
Oh, Ruko!

174
00:11:22,080 --> 00:11:25,080
Where's Hito-e? Is she okay?

175
00:11:25,080 --> 00:11:27,080
Uh, yeah, everything is just fine.

176
00:11:27,080 --> 00:11:28,080
Mostly, at least.

177
00:11:28,080 --> 00:11:30,080
Seems like she's calmed down now.

178
00:11:30,080 --> 00:11:32,080
The doctor's with her.

179
00:11:32,080 --> 00:11:33,080
You can go inside.

180
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:40,080
Oh, no.

181
00:11:40,080 --> 00:11:42,080
I'm alright.

182
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:48,080
I'm just scared.

183
00:11:49,080 --> 00:11:51,080
Hito-e was...

184
00:11:51,080 --> 00:11:53,080
She was so sweet before.

185
00:11:53,080 --> 00:11:56,080
But now I don't know what's going on in her head.

186
00:11:56,080 --> 00:11:58,080
It's terrifying.

187
00:11:58,080 --> 00:12:00,080
What am I supposed to do?

188
00:12:00,080 --> 00:12:02,080
What can I do?

189
00:12:02,080 --> 00:12:04,080
It's like...

190
00:12:04,080 --> 00:12:06,080
I don't even know her anymore.

191
00:12:06,080 --> 00:12:08,080
I'm at a loss.

192
00:12:08,080 --> 00:12:09,080
Um...

193
00:12:25,080 --> 00:12:28,080
Hey, Yuzuki, can I take you to my place for now?

194
00:12:29,080 --> 00:12:30,080
This is all my fault...

195
00:12:30,080 --> 00:12:31,080
Huh?

196
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:33,200
I was the one who made her battle.

197
00:12:35,440 --> 00:12:39,360
Well, yeah, but you just wanted to help, right?

198
00:12:41,180 --> 00:12:46,000
Even though the truth was more than Hitoi could take, your intentions were still noble.

199
00:12:47,280 --> 00:12:48,320
Thank you, Ruko.

200
00:12:50,800 --> 00:12:54,640
Ah, I just realized this will be the second time you've stayed over.

201
00:12:54,640 --> 00:13:01,940
Oh, um, actually, before we go back, can we stop somewhere for a sec?

202
00:13:17,760 --> 00:13:20,300
Is this good? Can you see from here?

203
00:13:21,260 --> 00:13:21,820
Yeah.

204
00:13:21,820 --> 00:13:27,760
Well, if it isn't Yuzuki and Kazuki, are you stepping out?

205
00:13:27,920 --> 00:13:29,300
Just to the convenience store.

206
00:13:29,500 --> 00:13:31,960
Looks like we've got snow coming, so be careful.

207
00:13:32,240 --> 00:13:32,820
Yes, ma'am.

208
00:13:33,240 --> 00:13:33,760
See you later.

209
00:13:41,700 --> 00:13:43,060
Yuzuki, something bothering you?

210
00:13:43,060 --> 00:13:43,120
No.

211
00:13:51,820 --> 00:13:57,120
What's this about?

212
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:00,940
I want to be boyfriend and girlfriend.

213
00:14:00,940 --> 00:14:09,900
This is the only time we can be together as lovers.

214
00:14:10,700 --> 00:14:13,120
Mom and dad are still upstairs watching TV.

215
00:14:13,520 --> 00:14:15,200
No one from school's here to see us.

216
00:14:15,900 --> 00:14:20,660
In weather like this, if we happen to share an umbrella, no one will bat an eye, right?

217
00:14:20,660 --> 00:14:23,540
No one from school's home.

218
00:14:25,800 --> 00:14:27,060
What?

219
00:14:27,060 --> 00:14:27,420
What now?

220
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:33,480
What now?

221
00:14:41,180 --> 00:14:41,960
What?

222
00:14:41,960 --> 00:14:59,160
Oh, isn't it beautiful, Kazuki?

223
00:14:59,700 --> 00:15:01,020
Snowing just for us.

224
00:15:06,940 --> 00:15:08,800
You really are strong, huh?

225
00:15:08,800 --> 00:15:12,100
You've been like that ever since we were little.

226
00:15:12,920 --> 00:15:15,900
You always protected me, kept me on the right path.

227
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:20,500
I should have told you.

228
00:15:21,560 --> 00:15:24,340
For my entire life, I've loved you.

229
00:15:30,680 --> 00:15:36,640
Thank you, but I want to protect you now, as your brother and your boyfriend.

230
00:15:38,800 --> 00:15:40,260
Hmm.

231
00:15:52,260 --> 00:16:08,340
She made my wish come true, didn't she?

232
00:16:08,340 --> 00:16:12,380
Even though she took my body, she still kept her word.

233
00:16:15,220 --> 00:16:16,460
Thank you, Hana-yo.

234
00:16:18,260 --> 00:16:19,620
You were my friend.

235
00:16:35,620 --> 00:16:37,540
You still...

236
00:16:37,540 --> 00:16:45,100
Setting your little plan into motion, are you?

237
00:16:45,260 --> 00:16:45,920
That's right.

238
00:16:46,640 --> 00:16:48,900
I wonder. You think she'll really come?

239
00:16:49,340 --> 00:16:51,280
Oh, don't worry. She'll come.

240
00:16:52,520 --> 00:16:53,720
She's the same as me.

241
00:16:54,560 --> 00:16:56,000
I suppose that's true.

242
00:16:56,420 --> 00:16:59,900
And by that, I mean you both have Wecross on the brain and not much else.

243
00:17:00,360 --> 00:17:01,980
Nothing personal, of course.

244
00:17:01,980 --> 00:17:06,320
Though I wonder if two of you might be one too many.

245
00:17:06,320 --> 00:17:11,540
That doesn't matter. She's my friend.

246
00:17:11,960 --> 00:17:15,560
If I have to sacrifice her, then I might as well just disappear.

247
00:17:16,340 --> 00:17:18,080
We're all still friends.

248
00:17:19,080 --> 00:17:21,540
She made my wish come true, didn't she?

249
00:17:22,680 --> 00:17:25,580
Even though she took my body, she still kept her word.

250
00:17:25,580 --> 00:17:32,300
If my wish came true, then my wish.

251
00:17:32,300 --> 00:17:48,800
Oh, Ru. Is something the matter?

252
00:17:49,280 --> 00:17:51,400
Uh, no, I'm fine. Just spacing out.

253
00:17:51,760 --> 00:17:53,440
So what are you up to out here, Grandma?

254
00:17:53,440 --> 00:17:59,740
Nothing exciting. It started to snow, so I'm trying to dry off the potatoes I left outside.

255
00:18:00,240 --> 00:18:01,480
Here, let me help.

256
00:18:01,480 --> 00:18:07,840
Hey, Grandma.

257
00:18:08,540 --> 00:18:08,760
Hmm.

258
00:18:09,760 --> 00:18:17,460
All my life, I never really wanted to be anything or do anything, and I didn't really care if I had friends or not.

259
00:18:17,460 --> 00:18:23,260
I guess that's not really normal, so I can't blame you for worrying.

260
00:18:24,100 --> 00:18:26,020
But I've changed my mind now.

261
00:18:28,980 --> 00:18:29,460
Hmm.

262
00:18:29,460 --> 00:18:32,980
I made friends and realized I was wrong.

263
00:18:33,520 --> 00:18:35,260
We had fun. I was happy.

264
00:18:36,140 --> 00:18:37,460
I wanted to...

265
00:18:37,460 --> 00:18:39,480
I mean, I want to stay with them forever.

266
00:18:40,560 --> 00:18:42,240
So, I mean...

267
00:18:42,240 --> 00:18:46,080
I guess what I'm asking is if there's anything I can do for them.

268
00:18:48,300 --> 00:18:48,780
Hmm.

269
00:18:49,860 --> 00:18:52,280
I'm sure you'll come up with something on your own.

270
00:18:52,280 --> 00:18:52,420
Huh?

271
00:18:53,140 --> 00:18:54,320
I have faith.

272
00:18:54,880 --> 00:18:56,700
You are my Ru, after all.

273
00:18:56,700 --> 00:18:59,220
You can do anything.

274
00:19:00,580 --> 00:19:01,460
Uh...

275
00:19:01,460 --> 00:19:02,460
Uh...

276
00:19:02,460 --> 00:19:04,840
Grandma.

277
00:19:05,880 --> 00:19:07,020
Now let's see.

278
00:19:07,400 --> 00:19:09,100
Guess we can't put them back outside.

279
00:19:09,700 --> 00:19:12,780
No, but maybe over there, where they can still get some sun.

280
00:19:12,980 --> 00:19:13,260
Okay.

281
00:19:19,980 --> 00:19:20,660
Toma?

282
00:19:21,880 --> 00:19:23,800
You're acting weird. What's wrong?

283
00:19:26,700 --> 00:19:34,060
I wonder if you were like me when you were a real girl.

284
00:19:36,200 --> 00:19:38,520
Bet you had all sorts of friends back then.

285
00:19:39,060 --> 00:19:40,580
It'd be fun to find out what kind of wish you...

286
00:19:40,580 --> 00:19:41,020
Stop it!

287
00:19:41,020 --> 00:19:43,940
I don't know, okay?

288
00:19:44,680 --> 00:19:46,840
I don't remember any of that stuff.

289
00:19:48,040 --> 00:19:48,900
I'm sorry.

290
00:19:49,260 --> 00:19:51,300
I didn't know that other stuff, either.

291
00:19:51,920 --> 00:19:55,860
Not about selector switching with L-Rigs or wishes or the weird room.

292
00:19:56,120 --> 00:19:57,220
I wouldn't lie to you.

293
00:19:57,440 --> 00:19:58,620
Please believe me, Ru.

294
00:19:58,680 --> 00:20:00,200
I just wanted to battle together.

295
00:20:00,260 --> 00:20:00,860
I promise.

296
00:20:02,480 --> 00:20:03,820
Of course I believe you.

297
00:20:05,320 --> 00:20:06,300
You mean it?

298
00:20:06,420 --> 00:20:06,820
Uh-huh.

299
00:20:07,120 --> 00:20:08,080
You're my friend.

300
00:20:08,420 --> 00:20:09,840
We have to trust each other.

301
00:20:09,840 --> 00:20:13,620
I guess you were right.

302
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:18,760
It sure has been a long day, huh?

303
00:20:19,960 --> 00:20:21,100
I'm going to bed.

304
00:20:24,240 --> 00:20:25,460
Night-night, Toma.

305
00:20:25,460 --> 00:20:43,860
Hey, did you see this?

306
00:20:43,860 --> 00:20:46,100
Yeah, the Iona fan event thing, right?

307
00:20:47,020 --> 00:20:47,260
Huh?

308
00:20:47,840 --> 00:20:50,640
But on the ad, it said it's only for select people.

309
00:20:50,740 --> 00:20:52,620
Do you have to win a contest or something?

310
00:20:52,760 --> 00:20:54,440
It didn't seem like it, but I don't know.

311
00:20:54,540 --> 00:20:56,040
There's no address listed, either.

312
00:20:56,800 --> 00:20:58,600
It doesn't list anything but a contact.

313
00:20:58,960 --> 00:20:59,600
Oh, yeah.

314
00:21:00,280 --> 00:21:03,000
I sent them an email about it, but I didn't get a reply.

315
00:21:03,360 --> 00:21:04,100
What the heck?

316
00:21:04,100 --> 00:21:05,940
Ruko!

317
00:21:07,880 --> 00:21:09,480
We gotta find that thing.

318
00:21:09,640 --> 00:21:10,680
Do a search for it.

319
00:21:10,760 --> 00:21:11,000
Uh-huh.

320
00:21:11,460 --> 00:21:13,620
Try typing Iona fan event.

321
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:14,980
Uh, right.

322
00:21:17,880 --> 00:21:24,320
What is it, Ru?

323
00:21:24,320 --> 00:21:29,880
An Iona fan event, just like they said.

324
00:21:30,560 --> 00:21:37,140
To those who are forced to select, to those who do not refuse to select, then it has hashtag

325
00:21:37,140 --> 00:21:38,260
selector at the bottom.

326
00:21:39,180 --> 00:21:41,540
So what do you guys think she's trying to do?

327
00:21:41,540 --> 00:21:44,160
She's calling us out.

328
00:21:44,840 --> 00:21:46,540
She's bringing the selectors together.

329
00:21:46,540 --> 00:22:16,520
Iona fan event, just like they said.

330
00:22:16,540 --> 00:22:46,520
Iona fan event, just like they said.

331
00:22:46,540 --> 00:23:16,520
Iona fan event, just like they said.

332
00:23:16,540 --> 00:23:25,820
Iona fan event, just like they said.

333
00:23:25,820 --> 00:23:27,840
It's happening really close to here, too.

334
00:23:28,400 --> 00:23:29,500
Is something wrong?

335
00:23:29,540 --> 00:23:32,140
I don't want to hear it, and I have nothing to say to you.

336
00:23:32,480 --> 00:23:34,060
I'm sure my plan is going to work.

337
00:23:34,380 --> 00:23:35,720
No, I don't want to!

338
00:23:36,060 --> 00:23:37,360
I finally thought of a wish.

339
00:23:37,760 --> 00:23:39,800
Next time, the summer of dreams.

